E4A5                             ;  Machine code: the grave
E4A5                             ; =============================================================================
E4A5                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E4A5                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E4A5                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E4A5                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E4A5                             ; contract in the header.
E4A5   20 E5 E4     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E4A8   B0 2D                  BCS   exec   
E4AA   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E4AB   0A                     ASL      
E4AC   0A                     ASL      
E4AD   0A                     ASL      
E4AE   85 04                  STA   T0   
